0905.0794	open_problem	The idea that two Boolean functions with disjoint spectra can be used to construct highly nonlinear resilient functions was clearly mentioned in \cite:933eab001f4bf37933a7f59bfc5e8b1c1518226c, and it was also used in \cite:aff1d8d3865d2e92f793698737ca8441ed20e324, \cite:0adad1a01afbb515b2d00ab31e763455a29ae2d2, \cite:d75e9b1fafccb6dc8079a7253451b4dc572952c3.	"Disjoint spectra functions will play an important role in constructing almost optimal resilient functions in this paper. Definition 3: A set of Boolean functions \(\{f_1, \ldots, f_m\}\) such that for any \(i \neq j\), \(W_{f_i}(\alpha) W_{f_j}(\alpha) = 0\) is called a set of disjoint spectra functions. The idea that two Boolean functions with disjoint spectra can be used to construct highly nonlinear resilient functions was clearly mentioned in \cite:933eab001f4bf37933a7f59bfc5e8b1c1518226c, and it was also used in \cite:aff1d8d3865d2e92f793698737ca8441ed20e324, \cite:0adad1a01afbb515b2d00ab31e763455a29ae2d2, \cite:d75e9b1fafccb6dc8079a7253451b4dc572952c3. In this section, we provide a simple construction method for a large set of disjoint spectra functions by using a set of “partially linear"" functions."	0.9
